index c2e05e17cbb9fe1b0dda1a53b293eda68cd96f2c..63bfd4fe4951841bd10882c42b2c62172964d74c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -651,3 +651,34 @@ $config = [
 ];
 $ydb = new \YdbPlatform\Ydb\Ydb($config);
 ```
+
+### Managed discovery long polling
+
+Enable both `discovery` and `discoveryLongPoll` to keep one conditional
+`ListEndpoints` request on the bootstrap connection. The synchronous driver
+processes completed polls before dispatch and while consuming streaming results.
+A new route closes the previous data channel shared by the driver's service
+clients. For idle workers, pass the running ReactPHP `LoopInterface` as
+`discoveryLoop` (requires PHP 7.4+). The loop checks for a completed poll every
+100 ms using the same bootstrap connection. A synchronous process without a
+running loop processes the update on its next SDK call or stream read. A
+blocking native gRPC receive also pauses the loop until a message, error, or
+RPC deadline arrives. During that pause the old socket stays open. On return the SDK checks for an
+available discovery response before yielding data. Once a response has started
+it waits for its generation trailers within the discovery timeout.
+After a switch, acquire a fresh session with `Table::session()`. A retained
+session raises `BadSessionException`. A file pool can reuse idle sessions after
+restart when the bootstrap, database, selected endpoint and managed generation
+match. Concurrent processes use independent sessions while one process holds the
+cache file. An opt-in driver with an unstamped server keeps its sessions in
+memory. Ordinary discovery keeps its existing file format. When an opaque
+custom pool is shared or returns an unrecognized ID, the driver uses its own
+memory pool for subsequent sessions.
+
+Legacy servers use the configured discovery interval. The opt-in requires a
+host:port endpoint, HTTP/2 support in libcurl, and default gRPC channel options.
+TLS uses `root_cert_file`, `GRPC_DEFAULT_SSL_ROOTS_FILE_PATH`, or the gRPC PHP
+package's bundled roots. If the process has already installed an in-memory gRPC
+root bundle, provide its file explicitly. Bootstrap honors gRPC's HTTP CONNECT
+proxy and bypass environment variables. Address-based gRPC proxy mapping
+requires native periodic discovery.
